# web_server.py — mount /api/explain (brain explain feature)

This patch records the manual edit applied to
`hermes_cli/web_server.py` (in the installed `hermes-agent` pip package)
to mount the `/api/explain` streaming endpoint.

## Why a patch file (not a git-tracked source edit)

`web_server.py` lives in the `hermes-agent` pip package, not in this
repo. The repo only carries deployment glue (`entrypoint.sh`,
`Dockerfile`, `skills/`, `hermes_explain.py`). The change is applied
in-place at the installed package location and re-applied idempotently
by `entrypoint.sh` on every container start (so a `hermes-agent` version
bump doesn't silently drop the endpoint). This file is the human-readable
record of intent; `entrypoint.sh` is the source of truth at runtime.

## Divergence from the original plan

The original plan assumed `start_server()` built and `return app`'d an
app instance, and inserted the mount before that `return app`. The real
`web_server.py` structure is different:

- `app` is a **module-level global** (`app = FastAPI(...)` near the top).
- Routes are mounted at **module import time** (no `build_app`/`return app`).
- `_mount_plugin_api_routes()` and `app.include_router(_dashboard_auth_router)`
  run at import scope, followed by `mount_spa(app)`.

There is no `return app` to insert before. The mount is inserted at module
scope, between the dashboard-auth router and `mount_spa(app)`. This
location is **load-bearing**: `mount_spa(app)` installs a
`/{full_path:path}` catch-all that would swallow `/api/explain` if the
mount came after it.

## The edit (unified-diff shape; re-derive line numbers against the live file)

The block is inserted immediately after:

    from hermes_cli.dashboard_auth.routes import router as _dashboard_auth_router  # noqa: E402
    app.include_router(_dashboard_auth_router)

and immediately before:

    mount_spa(app)

--- a/hermes_cli/web_server.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/web_server.py
@@ -18724,6 +18724,18 @@
 from hermes_cli.dashboard_auth.routes import router as _dashboard_auth_router  # noqa: E402
 app.include_router(_dashboard_auth_router)

+# ─── /api/explain — streaming code explanation (brain explain feature) ────────
+# Mounted before mount_spa() because the SPA installs a /{full_path:path}
+# catch-all that would otherwise swallow /api/explain. Routes are appended
+# directly (not mounted as a sub-app at /api) to avoid shadowing the existing
+# /api/plugins/* and /api/auth/* routes. See hermes_explain.build_explain_app.
+try:
+    from hermes_cli.hermes_explain import build_explain_app as _build_explain_app
+    for _r in _build_explain_app().routes:
+        app.routes.append(_r)
+    _log.info("Mounted /api/explain (code-explainer)")
+except Exception as _exc:  # noqa: BLE001
+    _log.warning("Failed to mount /api/explain: %s", _exc)
+
 mount_spa(app)

## Notes

- The import is package-qualified (`from hermes_cli.hermes_explain import ...`)
  because `hermes_cli/` is not on `sys.path` at runtime — only the
  `hermes_cli` package itself is importable. `entrypoint.sh` copies
  `hermes_explain.py` into the installed `hermes_cli/` package dir so this
  import resolves.
- Route-append (`app.routes.append(r)`) is used instead of
  `app.mount("/api", sub_app)` to avoid shadowing `/api/plugins/*` and
  `/api/auth/*`.
- The whole block is wrapped in `try/except` so a failure to build the
  explain app (e.g. missing `run_agent` import) doesn't take down the
  entire dashboard — it logs a warning and continues.
